# memory-homes.conf — per-repo CANONICAL memory dir (machine-INDEPENDENT).
# Copy to claude/memory-homes.conf (or point MEMORY_HOMES_CONF at your copy).
#
# Format: <repo-shortname> <memory-dir>   (one per line, # = comment)
# <memory-dir> may use ~ or $HOME; both expand to the real home.
#
# This is the dir Claude Code loads as its autoMemoryDirectory. Keep it inside
# your dotfiles tree and the layout is identical on every machine, so ONE value
# works everywhere (unlike transcript dirs, which encode the per-user cwd and
# live in memory-canonicals.conf).
#
# dream promotes here; session-analyzer writes <memory-dir>/.analysis/ here;
# reflections keeps <memory-dir>/reflections/<host>.jsonl here. Repos absent
# from this file use identities/<DF_IDENTITY>/claude/memory/<repo>/ for
# reflections, and the legacy <transcript-dir>/memory for dream/analyzer output.
#
# The memory tree holds what your agents learned about your work: sync it only
# through a PRIVATE repository (the public .gitignore keeps it out of a fork).
# See docs/memory/README.md.

webapp   ~/.dotfiles/identities/example/claude/memory/webapp
dotfiles ~/.dotfiles/identities/example/claude/memory/dotfiles
